{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-competitions-faq
  The competitions page FAQ: up to seven question/answer pairs as native
  <details>/<summary> accordions (no JS, answers stay in the DOM) plus the
  matching FAQPage JSON-LD built from the SAME resolved list, so the markup can
  never say something the page does not show. Built 2026-10-08 after the FAQ
  lived as JSON-LD only inside theinmag-competitions.liquid (a Google guideline
  breach: FAQ markup must match visible content) and after a first visible
  version inside that section was moved here by Ryan: the FAQ sits BELOW the
  mag promo (funnel strip), as the last thing on the page.

  LIVE DATA IN THE ANSWERS (2026-11-10, Ryan's go). Answers are templates with
  tokens that resolve at render time from the competitions data snippet, so the
  FAQ can no longer go stale between Compton's Tuesday passes:
    [live_count]    comps open right now (same expiry rule as the board: the
                    build-time tile state, downgraded if the ISO closing date
                    has passed, midnight to midnight)
    [free_count]    the subset of those whose cost slug is free
    [closing_names] comps open right now whose closing date falls in the
                    RENDER month, collected in the same expiry loop (so a comp
                    that closed yesterday drops out the same day its tile
                    does), soonest first because the build already sorts
                    live-now rows by closing date, as a reading list capped at
                    three: "A", "A and B", "A, B and C", "A, B and N more". Same
                    shape as _reading_list() in build-competitions-data.py, so
                    on push day it equals comp_closing_this_month_names in the
                    snippet (Compton's Tuesday check compares the two). The
                    snippet variable itself is NOT read here: it is frozen at
                    build time and would name a closed comp until the next push.
    [opening_names] comp_opening_soon_names from the snippet (opening dates
                    arriving between pushes wait for the rebuild, exactly as the
                    board's own "opens soon" tiles do)
    [updated]       comp_data_updated (the sweep date)
    [month]         the render month, full name
  GUARD: a pair is skipped, on the page AND in the JSON-LD, when its answer
  still holds an unfilled token, when it needs a names list that is blank,
  when it quotes [live_count] and that count is zero, or when it says "Most
  are" ([free_count]) and free is not more than half of live. Answers stay
  under 40 words as templates.

  Background: the field-notes index treatment (a drawn-pattern asset tiled at
  640px over a base colour under a cream wash), same settings as the funnel
  strip's tile mode so the two bands read as one surface. No Post heading:
  Ryan pulled it. The H2 is a question (AEO rule) in Inter.

  Answers are plain text settings and may carry <a href> links (Google allows
  them in FAQ answer text). They are the page's internal links to send-in and
  the gallery. No en or em dashes, ever. Ranges read "to".
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- include 'theinmag-competitions-data' -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: "got a question about kids' competitions?"
  assign faq_pairs = '1,2,3,4,5,6,7' | split: ','

  comment
    Render-time counts. Mirrors the board's comp_live_states rule exactly:
    compare the DATE string to the render date (midnight to midnight) so a comp
    closing today still counts as open all day.
  endcomment
  assign today_stamp = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | date: '%s' | times: 1
  assign now_ym = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m'
  assign live_count = 0
  assign free_count = 0
  assign closing_total = 0
  assign closing_first_two = ''
  assign closing_third = ''
  for id in comp_ids
    assign ci = forloop.index0
    assign cstate = comp_tile_states[ci]
    assign cexpiry = comp_expiry_dates[ci]
    if cexpiry != blank and cstate != 'annual-again'
      assign cexpiry_stamp = cexpiry | date: '%s' | times: 1
      if cexpiry_stamp < today_stamp
        assign cstate = 'annual-again'
      endif
    endif
    if cstate == 'live-now'
      assign live_count = live_count | plus: 1
      if comp_cost_slugs[ci] == 'free'
        assign free_count = free_count | plus: 1
      endif
      if cexpiry != blank
        assign cexpiry_ym = cexpiry | date: '%Y-%m'
        if cexpiry_ym == now_ym
          assign closing_total = closing_total | plus: 1
          if closing_total <= 2
            assign closing_first_two = closing_first_two | append: comp_names[ci] | append: '~~'
          elsif closing_total == 3
            assign closing_third = comp_names[ci]
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  assign live_count_text = live_count | append: ''
  assign free_count_text = free_count | append: ''
  assign free_twice = free_count | times: 2

  assign closing_names = ''
  if closing_total > 0
    assign closing_parts = closing_first_two | split: '~~'
    if closing_total == 1
      assign closing_names = closing_parts[0]
    elsif closing_total == 2
      assign closing_names = closing_parts[0] | append: ' and ' | append: closing_parts[1]
    elsif closing_total == 3
      assign closing_names = closing_parts[0] | append: ', ' | append: closing_parts[1] | append: ' and ' | append: closing_third
    else
      assign closing_more = closing_total | minus: 2
      assign closing_names = closing_parts[0] | append: ', ' | append: closing_parts[1] | append: ' and ' | append: closing_more | append: ' more'
    endif
  endif

  assign now_month = 'now' | date: '%B'
  assign updated_text = comp_data_updated | default: ''
  assign opening_names = ''
  if comp_opening_soon_names != blank
    assign opening_names = comp_opening_soon_names
  endif

  comment
    Resolve the pairs ONCE into two parallel lists, then render the visible
    accordions and the JSON-LD from the same lists.
  endcomment
  assign faq_sep = '~~|~~'
  assign final_qs = ''
  assign final_as = ''
  for n in faq_pairs
    assign q_key = 'faq_q' | append: n
    assign a_key = 'faq_a' | append: n
    assign q = section.settings[q_key]
    assign a = section.settings[a_key]
    if q == blank or a == blank
      continue
    endif
    if a contains '[closing_names]' and closing_names == blank
      continue
    endif
    if a contains '[opening_names]' and opening_names == blank
      continue
    endif
    if a contains '[updated]' and updated_text == blank
      continue
    endif
    if a contains '[live_count]' and live_count == 0
      continue
    endif
    if a contains '[free_count]' and free_twice <= live_count
      continue
    endif
    assign a = a | replace: '[live_count]', live_count_text
    assign a = a | replace: '[free_count]', free_count_text
    assign a = a | replace: '[closing_names]', closing_names
    assign a = a | replace: '[opening_names]', opening_names
    assign a = a | replace: '[updated]', updated_text
    assign a = a | replace: '[month]', now_month
    if a contains '['
      continue
    endif
    assign final_qs = final_qs | append: q | append: faq_sep
    assign final_as = final_as | append: a | append: faq_sep
  endfor
  assign final_q_list = final_qs | split: faq_sep
  assign final_a_list = final_as | split: faq_sep

  assign tile_src = ''
  if section.settings.tile_filename != blank
    assign tile_src = section.settings.tile_filename | asset_url
  endif
  assign tile_color = section.settings.tile_color | default: '#FFD99B'
  assign tile_wash = section.settings.tile_wash | default: 55
  assign tile_alpha = tile_wash | divided_by: 100.0
  capture section_style
    echo '--cfaq-color: '
    echo tile_color
    echo ';'
    if tile_src != blank
      echo ' --cfaq-image: '
      if tile_wash > 0
        echo 'linear-gradient(rgba(251, 246, 234, '
        echo tile_alpha
        echo '), rgba(251, 246, 234, '
        echo tile_alpha
        echo ')), '
      endif
      echo "url('"
      echo tile_src
      echo "');"
    endif
  endcapture
-%}

{%- if final_q_list.size > 0 -%}
<section
  class="theinmag-cfaq{% if tile_src != blank %} theinmag-cfaq--tile{% endif %}"
  aria-labelledby="theinmag-cfaq-heading-{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style }}"
  data-cfaq-live="{{ live_count }}"
  data-cfaq-free="{{ free_count }}"
  data-cfaq-closing="{{ closing_total }}"
>
  <div class="theinmag-cfaq__inner">
    <h2 id="theinmag-cfaq-heading-{{ section.id }}" class="theinmag-cfaq__heading">{{ heading }}</h2>
    {%- for q in final_q_list -%}
      {%- assign a = final_a_list[forloop.index0] -%}
        <details class="theinmag-cfaq__qa">
          <summary class="theinmag-cfaq__q">
            <span>{{ q }}</span>
            <svg class="theinmag-cfaq__chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="4,7 10,13 16,7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="theinmag-cfaq__a"><p>{{ a }}</p></div>
        </details>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for q in final_q_list -%}
      {%- assign a = final_a_list[forloop.index0] -%}
        {%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": {{ q | json }},
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ a | json }} }
        }
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- stylesheet -%}
  .theinmag-cfaq {
    background-color: var(--cfaq-color, #FFD99B);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px) clamp(44px, 6vw, 72px);
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq--tile {
    background-image: var(--cfaq-image);
    background-size: 640px auto;
    background-position: top center;
    background-repeat: repeat;
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__inner {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__heading {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__qa {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__qa:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: clamp(14px, 2vw, 20px) 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .theinmag-cfaq__q:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__chev {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__qa[open] .theinmag-cfaq__chev { transform: rotate(180deg); }
  .theinmag-cfaq__a {
    padding: 0 0 clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 22px);
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.9);
  }
  .theinmag-cfaq__a p { margin: 0; }
  .theinmag-cfaq__a a {
    color: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-cfaq__chev { transition: none; }
  }
{%- endstylesheet -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Competitions FAQ",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading (a question)", "default": "got a question about kids' competitions?" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Background (field notes index treatment)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tile_filename", "label": "Tiled texture filename", "default": "teacher_backgroundFAQ.jpg", "info": "Drawn-pattern image in /assets/, tiled at 640px over the colour below, under a cream wash. Empty = flat colour." },
    { "type": "color", "id": "tile_color", "label": "Base colour", "default": "#FFD99B" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "tile_wash", "label": "Wash (soften pattern)", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 55 },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Questions (also emitted as FAQPage JSON-LD)", "info": "Answers are templates under 40 words. Tokens fill from the competitions data at render time: [live_count] [free_count] [closing_names] [opening_names] [updated] [month]. A pair whose answer keeps an unfilled token, or needs a names list that is empty this week, is skipped on the page and in the schema. No en or em dashes; ranges read 'to'." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q1", "label": "Q1", "default": "What kids competitions are running in Australia right now?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a1", "label": "A1", "default": "[live_count] Australian kids' competitions are open for entries right now, each checked against its official page. Pick a category, filter by age and state, then click through to enter. New comps land most weeks." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q2", "label": "Q2", "default": "Are kids competitions in Australia free to enter?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a2", "label": "A2", "default": "Most are. [free_count] of the [live_count] open right now cost nothing to enter. The rest charge a small fee, or run a free option beside a paid one. Every tile shows the cost before you click through." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q3", "label": "Q3", "default": "Can my child enter competitions from any state in Australia?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a3", "label": "A3", "default": "Many are national, open to kids anywhere in Australia. Some are state only, usually run by a state government, library network or council. Use the state filter to see your state's comps first, with the national ones underneath." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q4", "label": "Q4", "default": "What kinds of kids competitions are listed here?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a4", "label": "A4", "default": "Art, photography, film, writing, poetry, STEM, performance and social good. theINmag's own open call is here too: <a href=\"/pages/send-in\">send in</a> a drawing, story or comic and it could be printed. See other kids' published creations in the <a href=\"/pages/gallery\">gallery</a>." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q5", "label": "Q5", "default": "How often is this list of competitions updated?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a5", "label": "A5", "default": "Weekly. Every closing date and entry link is checked against its official page on a regular sweep, last done [updated]. Spotted one we missed? Use the suggest-a-comp button at the top of the board." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q6", "label": "Q6", "default": "Which kids competitions close this month?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a6", "label": "A6", "default": "Closing in [month]: [closing_names]. Each date comes straight from the organiser's page and sits on the tile, so get entries in before it." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_q7", "label": "Q7", "default": "Which kids competitions open soon?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "faq_a7", "label": "A7", "default": "Opening next: [opening_names]. They are already on the board, so your kid can start making before entries open." }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "Competitions FAQ", "category": "Pages" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
